\newlabel{fig:dag_scenarios}{{S3}{74}{Directed acyclic graphs (DAGs) for the source-selection mechanisms in Sc1--Sc3. In this schematic, $D$ denotes data source (trial or historical), $Z$ treatment assignment, $Y$ an individual outcome, $X$ the measured predictors relevant to the depicted paths and $U$ unmeasured prognostic variables; participant and group indices are suppressed. Sc1: measured covariates predict the outcome but do not influence source selection. Sc2: measured covariates influence both source selection and outcome. Sc3: unmeasured variables influence source selection and outcome, and generate observed proxies through $U\to X$, with proxy association indexed by $\rho $. Other measured predictors are omitted from the schematic. The $D\to Z$ edge reflects that historical observations are controls, whereas treatment is assigned within the trial. These diagrams illustrate the simulation mechanisms, not an established causal structure for the clinical application}{figure.caption.13}{}}
\newlabel{fig:regional}{{S4}{75}{Separate-treatment model: regional historical shifts for Gaussian outcomes (Sc5). Historical outcomes are shifted upward by $\delta =0.5,1,2$ where $X_5\leq 2$, and are unshifted otherwise. (a) Posterior probability of a small discrepancy, $P\{|g(x)|<0.5\mid \text {data}\}$. (b) Posterior mean discrepancy; dashed lines show the true trial-minus-historical discrepancy, $-\delta $ in the shifted region and zero elsewhere. Solid curves summarize pooled trial-control profiles within $X_5$ bins of width 0.5 across 40 replicates; they are not uncertainty intervals. The dotted line marks the shift boundary. Primary lrcBART uses $H_f=50$, $H_g=5$, $w\sim \operatorname {Beta}(1,1)$ and requested prior ESS 100}{figure.caption.14}{}}

